        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            DIY materials for a deck strip run roughly $0.20 to $0.60 per square foot of treated surface, which is $120 to $350 on most decks and rises towards $0.90 on a painted one. A professional strip and re-stain is $2.50 to $5.00 per square foot, and the gap is labour rather than markup: this is slow, physical work done on your knees.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before committing either way, spend ten minutes on a test patch. The finish type and the coat count determine whether this is a cheap weekend or a fortnight, and on a heavily painted deck they also determine whether stripping beats simply replacing the boards. That is the comparison worth running, and almost nobody runs it before buying the first gallon.
          </p>
